    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0717" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/5–2446</note>
                <head>No. 397<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Briefing Book Paper</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d397-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">East Prussia</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">a.</hi>
                    </label>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Recommendation:</hi>—East Prussia (except for the
                        Koenigsberg district, which presumably will go to the Soviet Union) should
                        be ceded to Poland.</item>
                    <label>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">b.</hi>
                    </label>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Basic Data:</hi>— …</item>
                    <label/>
                    <item>… The whole of East Prussia is claimed by the Warsaw Polish Government.
                        The Soviet Union favors Polish acquisition of East Prussia or all of the
                        province except for the northeastern sector, including the chief city and
                        part [<hi rendition="#italic">port</hi>] of Koenigsberg which it intends to
                        annex. … </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-30">June 30,
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d397-f1" n="1" xml:id="d397-f1-content">
                <p>For the full text of this briefing paper, see attachment 1 to <ref target="#d513"
                        >document No. 513</ref>.</p>
            </note>
